        "id": 7597,
        "name": "Tridens",
        "username": "Tridens",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/3e96dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-05T18:10:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi, I'm new to Sentinels (three games and loving it).&nbsp; I have a rules question involving the interaction between Interpolation Beam (IB) and Impromptu Invention (I2).&nbsp; IB deals damage every time a player \"draws\" a hero card.&nbsp; I2 first says \"draw a card\" (IB clearly causes damage here).&nbsp; Then it says, \"Search your deck for an equipment card and either put it into play or your hand.\"&nbsp; So does this \"search\" trigger IB again?&nbsp; In other words, is a successful \"Search\" considered a \"Draw\"?</p><p>Thanks for your help.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:55.246Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 7594,
        "topic_slug": "interpolation-beam-and-impromptu-invention-draw-vs-search",
        "display_username": "Tridens",
        "primary_group_name": null,
